# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# IDEs
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Environment / secrets
.env
.env.local
*.key

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
dist/
*.egg-info/
# Decision logs are run artifacts, not source (docs/observability.md §3).
decisions.jsonl
*.decisions.jsonl

# Node (docs/mod tooling)
node_modules/

# C++ / CMake (engine builtin build output)
build/
*.o
*.obj

# GLSMAC debug dumps (when running the integration loop)
tmp/lastmap.*

# Agent runtime / session state
.runtime/
# .claude/settings.json and .claude/skills/ ARE read by cloud sessions (repo hooks
# and project skills carry over, user-level ~/.claude does not), so both are
# tracked. Everything else under .claude/ is local state.
#
# Skills belong in the repo for the same reason settings.json does, and for one
# more: a skill is how a harness learns to play this game. Leaving it untracked
# means a fresh checkout has the MCP surface and no instructions for using it —
# which is exactly the half that cannot be inferred from the code.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/skills/
.logs/
state.json
CLAUDE.local.md

# Beads / Dolt files (added by bd init)
.dolt/
*.db
.beads-credential-key
.beads/proxieddb/

# Graphs generated from YOUR OWN SMAC install are derived copyrighted game
# data and are never committed. The Thinker-sourced graph under
# datalinks/thinker/ is committed: it comes from the MIT-licensed fork's
# public repo and is tagged house-rule, not canonical.
# Root-anchored so it cannot swallow orchestrator/src/neural_amplifier/datalinks/.
/datalinks/*
!/datalinks/thinker/
# mechanics.ttl is hand-authored by this project and carries NO game data: it
# describes how the engine offers and applies orders, which no alphax.txt row
# states. It is not a derived copy of anything, so the copyright rule above does
# not reach it — and unlike thinker/, it must not be regenerated.
!/datalinks/mechanics.ttl

# Local Quipu store — rebuildable with `just quipu-load`.
/.quipu/

# Beads local working state (the tracked artifact is .beads/issues.jsonl)
.beads/.auto-import-issues.jsonl

# mdBook output — rebuildable with `just docs build`. The sources are docs/.
/book/

# Beads runtime lock
*.gate.lock*

# Fetched embedding model (na-6td). Never committed: ~90 MB of weights, the large-file
# pre-commit check would refuse it, and a vendored binary in a source tree is a licence and
# provenance question nobody wants to answer later. scripts/fetch-embedding-model.sh puts it
# here, and keeps whatever it could reach when the weights host is blocked.
models/

# bobbin tool telemetry — generated per-invocation, never a source artifact
.bobbin/
